.TH PAIN-CONTROL-REVAMPED 1 "2026-11-16" "pain-control-revamped" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pain-control-revamped \- pane and window keys for tmux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pain-control-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.B apply
.br
.B pain-control-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.B list
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B pain-control-revamped doctor
.br
.B pain-control-revamped version
.br
.B pain-control-revamped help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pain-control-revamped
binds keys for moving between panes, resizing them, splitting in the
current folder, swapping, joining, breaking and promoting panes, and
managing windows. Each key is checked against the tmux version, carries a
note that
.B prefix ?
shows, and can be left alone. The entry point
.B pain-control-revamped.tmux
runs
.B apply
once when tmux loads the plugin, and every binding goes to tmux in one call.
.PP
Run with no command on a terminal, it offers a menu.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Bind every key now.
.TP
.B list
Print every binding apply would make, one per line.
.TP
.B zoom
Move the active pane to a window of its own and leave a placeholder where it
was. Run again in the zoomed pane or in the placeholder, it puts the pane back
in its place, and any panes opened beside it stay in the zoom window. Needs
tmux 3.0.
.TP
.B doctor
Print one row per dependency: tmux,
.B ps
for vim navigation, gum and the core tools. Exits 1 only when a required tool
is missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, then the tmux version.
.TP
.B help
Print the help page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
.B list
prints one JSON object.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colours of the terminal interface:
.BR kodougu ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
.BR catppuccin\-latte ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR nord ,
.BR gruvbox ,
.B tokyo\-night
or
.BR mono .
The default is
.BR kodougu .
.TP
.BI \-\- setting " value"
Any tmux option under TMUX OPTIONS, named with dashes, such as
.B \-\-resize 3
or
.BR "\-\-join\-key J" .
.PP
Each option also takes the form
.IR \-\-name = value ,
and
.B \-\-
ends the options.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BI PAIN_CONTROL_REVAMPED_ SETTING
Any tmux option under TMUX OPTIONS in capitals, such as
.BR PAIN_CONTROL_REVAMPED_RESIZE .
An option wins over the environment, and the environment over the tmux
option; an empty value leaves the key unbound.
.TP
.B PAIN_CONTROL_REVAMPED_THEME
The theme when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B PAIN_CONTROL_REVAMPED_ACCENT
A colour such as #CBA6F7 that replaces the accent of the theme.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_THEME
The theme of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when neither
.B \-\-theme
nor
.B PAIN_CONTROL_REVAMPED_THEME
is set.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_ACCENT
The accent of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when
.B PAIN_CONTROL_REVAMPED_ACCENT
is not set.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off in every theme.
.SH TMUX OPTIONS
An empty tmux option means its default.
.TP
.B @pain_control_revamped_resize
Cells per resize step. The default is 5.
.TP
.B @pain_control_revamped_new_window_path
.B true
makes
.B c
open the new window in the pane's folder. The default is
.BR true .
.TP
.B @pain_control_revamped_disabled_keys
Keys to leave alone, separated by spaces or commas.
.TP
.B @pain_control_revamped_no_wrap
.B on
stops pane navigation at the window's edge. The default is
.BR off .
.TP
.B @pain_control_revamped_vim_navigation
.B on
binds C-h to C-l and C-\e without the prefix, sending them to vim when it runs
in the pane, or to any pane whose
.B @pane-is-vim
option is set, as smart-splits.nvim sets it. The default is
.BR off .
.TP
.B @pain_control_revamped_vim_pattern
The process names vim navigation treats as vim.
.TP
.B @pain_control_revamped_pane_titles
.B on
shows each pane's index and title on its border. The default is
.BR off .
.TP
.BR @pain_control_revamped_smart_split_key ", " _join_key ", " _break_key ", " _swap_prev_key ", " _swap_next_key ", " _promote_key ", " _mark_key ", " _swap_mark_key
Keys bound by default:
.BR * ,
.BR @ ,
.BR ! ,
.BR { ,
.BR } ,
.BR + ,
.B m
and
.BR = .
.TP
.BR @pain_control_revamped_sync_key ", " _swap_window_left_key ", " _swap_window_right_key ", " _move_window_key ", " _kill_window_key ", " _layout_even_h_key ", " _layout_even_v_key ", " _layout_main_v_key ", " _respawn_key ", " _capture_key ", " _pane_name_key ", " _scratch_key
Keys left unbound until set.
.TP
.B @pain_control_revamped_scratch_command
The command the scratch popup runs. The default is a shell.
.TP
.B @pain_control_revamped_zoom_key
The key that runs
.BR zoom .
Unbound until set.
.TP
.B @pain_control_revamped_focus_size
A whole number from 50 to 99: the percent of the window's width and height
the focused pane grows to after every pane selection and split, on tmux 3.1
and later. Unset, panes keep their size. Unsetting it takes effect when the
tmux server restarts.
.TP
.B @revamped_theme
The theme of every tmux-revamped tool, when nothing else sets one. The default
is
.BR kodougu .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1)
